@@ -69,6 +69,29 @@ making it possible to control Alacritty without directly accessing it.
 
 			Default: _$ALACRITTY_WINDOW_ID_
 
+*gutter-event* _<EVENT>_
+
+	Send a bounded semantic event to the terminal gutter. Events change only
+	the per-window visual overlay and never write to the terminal grid.
+
+	*ARGS*
+		*<EVENT>*
+
+			One of: _reset_, _codex-start_, _codex-stop_, _reasoning_,
+			_search_, _read_, _edit_, _tool_, _test_, _verify_, _complete_,
+			_failed_, _command-start_, _command-pass_, _command-fail_,
+			_campaign-launch_, _candidate-start_, _candidate-reject_,
+			_candidate-pass_, _qualification-start_, _qualified_,
+			_composition-start_, _composition-pass_, _wrench-start_, or
+			_wrench-reject_.
+
+	*OPTIONS*
+		*-w, --window-id* _<WINDOW_ID>_
+
+			Window ID for the gutter event.
+
+			Default: _$ALACRITTY_WINDOW_ID_
+
 *config*
 
 	Update the Alacritty configuration.
